# Gene Pollinator's second cost needs an untapped permanent besides the one its {T} taps: on turn 3, with the Mox Emerald
# (its only other permanent) tapped for mana, the ability is not offered, though Gene Pollinator itself is untapped and
# no longer summoning sick (it could not pay both costs with itself). The positive control is turn 5 here: the Mox Emerald has untapped, and Gene Pollinator taps it and itself for red mana.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Gene Pollinator
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Gene Pollinator.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
! Bot1.Battlefield.Gene Pollinator.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Gene Pollinator.Activate(Tap: Mox Emerald; Color: Red)
? Bot1.Mana = {R}
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Gene Pollinator.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Tapped = true
